        "reason": "Code is structurally sound. All imports (ServiceBusClient, ServiceBusMessage, ServiceBusReceivedMessage, ServiceBusSender, ServiceBusReceiver, ProcessErrorArgs) are valid exports from @azure/service-bus. tsconfig.json is well-configured. Could not run tsc due to environment restrictions but no type errors are apparent."
      },
      {
        "name": "Latest Package Versions",
        "passed": true,
        "reason": "package-lock.json resolves @azure/service-bus to 7.9.5, which matches the latest version on npm. TypeScript 5.9.3 and @types/node 20.19.39 are also current."
      },
      {
        "name": "Best Practices",
        "passed": false,
        "reason": "Uses connection strings instead of DefaultAzureCredential/@azure/identity for authentication. While the prompt requested connection string usage, Azure SDK best practice is identity-based auth. Cleanup via close() in finally blocks is good."
      },
      {
        "name": "Error Handling",
        "passed": false,
        "reason": "Only a top-level catch for fatal errors. No RestError handling, no retry configuration, no granular error handling for send/receive operations. The processError handler only logs but doesn't handle specific error types."
      },
      {
        "name": "Code Quality",
        "passed": true,
        "reason": "Well-structured with clear section comments, proper TypeScript types, async/await throughout, and logical orchestration in main(). Clean, readable, and well-organized."
      },
      {
        "name": "Correct @azure/ Scoped Packages",
        "passed": true,
        "reason": "Uses @azure/service-bus, which is the correct scoped package. No deprecated unscoped packages."
      },
      {
        "name": "@azure/identity for Authentication",
        "passed": false,
        "reason": "Does not include @azure/identity. Uses connection string authentication (new ServiceBusClient(connectionString)) with a fallback hardcoded placeholder string. No Entra token credential usage."
      },
      {
        "name": "Client Constructor with Endpoint and Credential",
        "passed": false,
        "reason": "ServiceBusClient is constructed with a connection string (new ServiceBusClient(connectionString)) rather than endpoint URL + credential object pattern."
      },
      {
        "name": "Async/Await Pattern",
        "passed": true,
        "reason": "All asynchronous operations use async/await consistently. Top-level main() is an async function called with .catch(). No callback patterns or raw .then() chains."
      },
      {
        "name": "Pagination with for-await-of",
        "passed": true,
        "reason": "Not applicable to Service Bus messaging — there are no list/query operations returning PagedAsyncIterableIterator in this scenario. Criterion is satisfied by non-applicability."
      },
      {
        "name": "LRO Pattern (beginXxx + pollUntilDone)",
        "passed": true,
        "reason": "Not applicable to Service Bus messaging — there are no long-running operations in this scenario. Criterion is satisfied by non-applicability."
      },
      {
        "name": "RestError Exception Handling",
        "passed": false,
        "reason": "No RestError import or catch block with statusCode inspection. Only generic Error catching in the top-level main().catch(). processError handler logs but doesn't inspect error types."
      },
      {
        "name": "No Deprecated Packages",
        "passed": true,
        "reason": "All dependencies are current @azure/* track packages. No deprecated packages like azure-storage, azure-arm-*, ms-rest-azure, etc."
      },
      {
        "name": "Logging via @azure/logger",
        "passed": false,
        "reason": "Does not import or use @azure/logger. No setLogLevel() call or AZURE_LOG_LEVEL environment variable configuration. Uses only console.log/console.error for output."
      },
      {
        "name": "package.json with Correct Dependencies",
        "passed": true,
        "reason": "Valid package.json with @azure/service-bus dependency. Includes tsconfig.json, TypeScript 5.4+, and @types/node for TypeScript support."
      },
      {
        "name": "@azure/service-bus npm package",
        "passed": true,
        "reason": "@azure/service-bus is listed in package.json dependencies and properly imported in the source file."
      },
      {
        "name": "ServiceBusClient constructor with connection string",
        "passed": true,
        "reason": "createClient() function creates new ServiceBusClient(connectionString) using environment variable or placeholder."
      },
      {
        "name": "createSender() for queue or topic",
        "passed": true,
        "reason": "client.createSender(queueName) and client.createSender(topicName) are both demonstrated."
      },
      {
        "name": "ServiceBusMessageBatch with tryAddMessage()",
        "passed": true,
        "reason": "sendBatchMessages() creates a batch via sender.createMessageBatch() and adds 5 messages using batch.tryAddMessage() with overflow checking."
      },
      {
        "name": "createReceiver() for queue or subscription",
        "passed": true,
        "reason": "client.createReceiver(queueName) for queue and client.createReceiver(topicName, subscriptionName) for subscription are both shown."
      },
      {
        "name": "receiveMessages() and subscribe() for streaming",
        "passed": true,
        "reason": "receiveAndCompleteMessages() uses receiver.receiveMessages(10, {maxWaitTimeInMs: 5000}). subscribeToMessages() uses receiver.subscribe() with processMessage and processError handlers."
      },
      {
        "name": "completeMessage(), abandonMessage(), deadLetterMessage()",
        "passed": false,
        "reason": "Only completeMessage() is demonstrated. abandonMessage() and deadLetterMessage() are never called or shown anywhere in the code."
      },
      {
        "name": "close() on sender, receiver, and client for cleanup",
        "passed": true,
        "reason": "Finally block calls sender.close(), receiver.close(), client.close(). Topic sender and subscription receiver are also closed in demonstrateTopicAndSubscription()."
      }
    ]
