  "summary": "The code is well-structured and demonstrates most Service Bus messaging patterns effectively. It correctly uses createMessageBatch/tryAddMessage for batching, receiveMessages for pull-based receive, subscribe for push-based streaming, and proper close() cleanup. Key weaknesses: uses connection strings instead of @azure/identity, lacks RestError handling, omits @azure/logger, and fails to demonstrate abandonMessage() and deadLetterMessage() which were explicitly required.",
  "issues": [
